+### Compile-free structured TensorIR preparation
+
+The private compiler layer has a compile-free preparation/finalization seam;
+it is not a Python API and is not yet wired into `Artifact.compile_strict()` or
+the private producer. `PrepareStructuredTensorIrCompilation(program, request,
+schedule)` is the sole constructor path for
+`PreparedStructuredTensorIrCompilation`. It calls `EmitTensorIr(program)`, then
+owns copies of the request and schedule, the resolved strict producer options,
+the exact canonical TensorIR source bytes, copied `Input0`, `Input1`, `Result0`
+metadata, and five canonical identity projections. `TensorIrModule` does not
+cross this seam, and the prepared value cannot be mixed with a different
+request or schedule during finalization.
+
+The prepared value is deliberately not a `KernelBuildSpec` and is not a cache
+key. The callable identity does not exist until finalization receives the real
+producer ABI, so `ArtifactCache.lookup()` is unavailable at the prepared stage.
+The compiler must not invent a provisional callable digest, publish or later
+rewrite a provisional key, or invoke the producer once to discover an ABI and
+again after a cache lookup. A future compile-avoiding lookup requires a
+separately versioned, deterministic producer-analysis contract that returns the
+complete callable ABI without generating device code; that analysis is not
+part of this seam.
+
+Every projection is canonical MessagePack v1 in lexical map-key order, capped
+at 1 MiB, and contains no binary, extension, or floating-point value:
+
+| KernelBuildSpec input | Contract | Contents |
+| --------------------- | -------- | -------- |
+| static specialization | `pypto.frontend.static_specialization.v1` | ordered argument/result roles, ordinals, and positive static HIR shapes |
+| symbolic specialization | `pypto.frontend.symbolic_specialization.v1` | explicit empty `constraints` and `symbols` arrays |
+| argument ABI | `pypto.frontend.argument_abi.v1` | ordered inputs with `direction=in`, dtype code/name, rank, static shape, logical dense strides, contiguous and explicit-stride state |
+| result ABI | `pypto.frontend.result_abi.v1` | ordered results with the same dtype/layout metadata, without an input direction |
+| mutation ABI | `pypto.frontend.mutation_abi.v1` | two read-only argument effects and one `nil` result alias |
+
+The sixth identity domain remains the SHA-256 of the raw canonical TensorIR
+source bytes, without a MessagePack envelope. A `nil` result alias means that
+the HIR/SSA result has no input-alias lineage; it does not claim runtime pointer
+non-overlap, C/C++ `restrict`, or a loader-side alias check.
+
+`FinalizeStructuredTensorIrBuildSpec(prepared, real_kernel_abi)` accepts no
+caller-provided callable digest. It validates the returned kernel ABI against
+the prepared metadata and schedule, then uses only
+`ArtifactKernelAbi.identity_digest` as `KernelBuildSpec.callable_abi_digest`.
+The v1 check requires the fixed runtime/entry names; exactly ordered tensor
+descriptors for `Input0`, `Input1`, `Result0`; fully static matching shapes and
+strides with no dynamic metadata; two inputs, three kernel pointer arguments,
+`uniform_signature=false`, and pointer-only packing; static grid policy driven
+by descriptor zero; exact schedule tile sizes; zero workspace; and the fixed
+launch and CUDA 13.0-minimum loader ABI.
+
+The producer ABI descriptors do not contain dtype or source-role fields. Dtype
+is bound by the exact TensorIR source and frontend argument/result projections;
+`Input0`, `Input1`, and `Result0` roles are inferred positionally from descriptor
+order and input count. This is deterministic identity validation, not an
+independent proof of dtype or role semantics from Cubin bytes.
+
+Static specialization binds HIR shapes, not launch-grid dimensions.
+Layout-propagation may flatten or normalize TensorIR iteration space, so this
+compile-free seam deliberately does not recompute an exact grid from HIR shape
+and tile sizes. It requires the producer-shaped one-dimensional layout
+`y=1,z=1` and a positive `x` within the copied request's target limit. The exact
+`x` remains producer-owned until a subsequent real-producer parity test freezes
+that normalized iteration-space result. This commit invokes no producer,
+filesystem, subprocess, CUDA API, or GPU.
+
